  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>freqspace</keyword>
  <short_description>Frequency spacing for frequency responses.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>f = freqspace(n)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>f = freqspace(n, 'whole')</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[f1, f2] = freqspace(n)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[f1, f2] = freqspace([m n])</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[x, y] = freqspace(..., 'meshgrid')</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>n</param_name>
      <param_description>number of points: a positive scalar, or <b>[m n]</b> for a 2-D response.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>'whole'</param_name>
      <param_description>returns <b>n</b> points around the whole unit circle.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>'meshgrid'</param_name>
      <param_description>returns 2-D grids instead of vectors.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>f</param_name>
      <param_description>normalized frequencies, 1 being the Nyquist frequency.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>f1, f2</param_name>
      <param_description>frequency vectors (or grids) along columns and rows.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>f = freqspace(n)</b> returns <b>(0:floor(n/2)) * 2/n</b>, and <b>f = freqspace(n, 'whole')</b> returns <b>(0:n-1) * 2/n</b>.</p>
    <p><b>[f1, f2] = freqspace(n)</b> returns centered frequencies <b>((0:n-1) - floor(n/2)) * 2/n</b> for a 2-D response. With <b>[m n]</b>, <b>f1</b> has <b>n</b> points and <b>f2</b> has <b>m</b> points.</p>
  </description>
